    <name>OpenLinkHub Client</name>
    <summary>Configure Corsair devices through OpenLinkHub</summary>
    <developer id="io.github.mdmatthias">
        <name>mdmatthias</name>
    </developer>
    <description>
        <p>
            A desktop client for OpenLinkHub, the open source Linux service for Corsair devices. It gives
            OpenLinkHub an iCUE-style interface: device artwork with clickable buttons, an action list and a
            settings panel. The client only talks to OpenLinkHub's HTTP API; OpenLinkHub must be running.
        </p>
        <p>Features:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Key remapping for mice, headsets, controllers and keyboards</li>
            <li>Keyboards drawn from the key layout OpenLinkHub sends</li>
            <li>DPI stages, lighting, fans and pumps, equalizer and device settings</li>
            <li>OpenLinkHub user profiles and the Slipstream receiver</li>
            <li>Login for OpenLinkHub instances with dashboard authentication</li>
            <li>Tray icon and built-in updates</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Not affiliated with or endorsed by Corsair.</p>
    </description>
